{"page_content": "Parameter Description Assessed waste treatment Municipal waste incineration process Coverage Waste collection, transport, temporary storage, feeding into the furnace and thermal treatment are covered. As MCCPs are not contained in bottom ashes or slags, no processing of secondary waste is considered. Sludge from wastewater is regarded as being disposed of by incineration or in hazardous waste landfills. Emission resulting from these processes are regarded as covered by the scenario due to a) insignificant emissions and b) conservativeness of assessment Types of wastes End-of-life sealants, carbonless copy paper Assumptions The process is operated according to the legal requirements. Pre-treatment No pre-treatment of wastes, except mechanical reduction of volume and mixing Physical form Contained in solid wastes Operational conditions Storage of waste in closed bunkers, operating temperatures according to waste and risk management incineration directive (850 + 1100), furnace is fully closed. measures The incinerator is equipped with wet flue-gas cleaning (washer) with an efficacy of 95% for MCCPs and an on-site WWTP with an efficacy of removal of MCCP from water of 70%. Secondary wastes (sludge) are disposed of in landfills or incinerated. Information on Operating days Number of plants installations 330 d/a 600 Maximum amount Use of sealants: EoL copy paper: EoL sealants: Total: 256.5 kg/d treated: Local scenario 7.773 kg/d 93.273 kg/d 155.454 kg/d Maximum amount 33.41 t/a treated: Regional scenario Water treatment On-site waste water treatment with effectiveness of at least 70% removal from waste water. For the exposure assessment, direct discharge to surface waters is to be assumed. Collection rate of initial 100% of flue gas enters washer releases 100% of water in washer enters WWTP Release factor to air RFair,initial = 0.0001 RFRMM = 0.05 RFair = 0.00005 Justification: high degree of Justification: efficacy decomposition, residual specified by release in fly ash manufacturer as 95% Release factor to water RFwater,initial = 0.000095 RFRMM = 0.3 RFwater = 0.0000285 Justification: emissions to air Justification: WWTP multiplied with efficacy of efficacy of 70% washer", "metadata": {"doc_id": "58563b00-c9fb-4835-bede-2ac39b9770a5", "content_type": "Table", "filename": "r18_v2_final_en.pdf"}}